    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.completion\n\n### Description\n\nIt would be nice to have different colored menu items for different types of completions, like snippets, functions, variables, etc. nvim-cmp supports this, but I couldn't find any docs that mentions this functionality for mini.completion.\n\nExample of what would be great to have:\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/bea35830-0af7-4681-8ed3-709791f62cd1)",
